    {
      "id": "p0125-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "For linguistic and historical reasons, the Japanese word 青 (ao) usually means \"blue\" in English, but can instead mean \"green\" in some situations. In general, ao means \"green\" when referring to plants, fruits, vegetables, and other types of \"vibrant\" green. Ao can also mean \"green\" in relation to other things, including stoplights and being new to something.",
        "raw": "For linguistic and historical reasons, the Japanese word ~ (ao) usually\nmeans \"blue\" in English, but can instead mean \"green\" in some situations.\nIn general, ao means \"green\" when referring to plants, fruits, vegetables,\nand other types of \"vibrant\" green. Ao can also mean \"green\" in relation\nto other things, including stoplights and being new to something.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.12313453,
          0.11727857,
          0.67666461,
          0.19623571
        ],
